      <Step>
      <strong>Read the elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;ditavalref href="…"&gt;</code> inside a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> applies that DITAVAL to the topicref and everything under it. One <code>&lt;ditavalref&gt;</code> filters the branch in place; two or more make one copy of the branch per DITAVAL. Here the branch is the install task and, nested under it, <em>Recording your first track</em>, so each platform gets both pages.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;ditavalmeta&gt;</code> holds the naming. <code>&lt;dvrResourcePrefix&gt;</code> is put before the file name of every copied topic, <code>&lt;dvrResourceSuffix&gt;</code> after it (before the extension). The Windows and Mac branches use a prefix, the Linux branch a suffix, so you see both forms in the output; in a real project pick one.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;dvrKeyscopePrefix&gt;</code> puts the copies in separate key scopes. The branch defines <code>install</code> and <code>first-track</code>; without the prefixes, three copies would define the same keys, and the first would win. With them the keys are <code>win.install</code>, <code>mac.install</code> and <code>linux.install</code>, and the same for <code>first-track</code>. Stage 17 is about key scopes.</li>
      <li>The rest of the map is what any root map needs: the scheme, the product and glossary keys, the shared topics.</li>
      <li>The <code>&lt;topicref toc="no"&gt;</code> to <code>audio-units.dita</code> is the same one the beginner map got in stage 14. <em>Recording your first track</em> links to pages that use <code>&lt;abbreviated-form&gt;</code>, and a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> to a fragment such as <code>audio-units.dita#gl-decibel</code> does not make DITA-OT publish the glossary group. The topicref publishes the group so that those links have a page to land on, and keeps it out of the table of contents.</li>
      <li>The <code>&lt;topicref toc="no"&gt;</code> to <code>supported-audio-formats.dita</code> does the same for the formats topic, and defines the key <code>formats</code>. The exporting task, which this map reaches through links, says "see <code>&lt;xref keyref="formats/choosing"/&gt;</code>". Without the key in this map, that reference resolves to nothing and the output reads "see )"; with only a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code>, the link resolves but the page is not published.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>List the branches</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml list-branches installation-variants.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"win-                 filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-windows.ditaval  keyscope=win.\nmac-                 filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-mac.ditaval  keyscope=mac.\n-linux               filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-linux.ditaval  keyscope=linux.\n3 branch variant(s)."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Each line is one variant: its prefix, the topic it filters, the DITAVAL and the key scope. A variant with no prefix is labeled by its suffix.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-the-deliverable-and-the-check" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: The deliverable and the check<a href="#step-3-the-deliverable-and-the-check" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Add the deliverable</strong> Choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Project Tools</strong> &gt; <strong>Manage Deliverables...</strong> and click <strong>Add...</strong>. Enter these values:
      <Table class="my-4">
      <TableHeader>
      <TableRow>
      <TableHead>Field</TableHead>
      <TableHead>Value</TableHead>
      </TableRow>
      </TableHeader>
      <TableBody>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Name</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>install-variants</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Input map</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>installation-variants.ditamap</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>DITAVAL (optional)</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell>(leave empty)</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Transtype</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>html5</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Output (optional)</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell><code>out/install-variants</code></TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      <TableRow>
      <TableCell><strong>Publication parameters</strong></TableCell>
      <TableCell>(none)</TableCell>
      </TableRow>
      </TableBody>
      </Table>
      <p>Leave <strong>DITAVAL</strong> empty: the <code>&lt;ditavalref&gt;</code> elements in the map do the filtering. Click <strong>Save...</strong>, click <strong>OK</strong> to write the deliverable, and click <strong>Close</strong>.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Preview a branch</strong> In the status bar's deliverable menu, choose <code>install-variants</code>. Open <code>topics/installing-audacity.dita</code> and choose <strong>View</strong> &gt; <strong>Preview in Tab</strong>. Because the map has branches, the bar above the preview adds <strong>Branch</strong>, set to <strong>Whole map</strong>. Choose <strong>win-</strong> and scroll to the install step: the preview applies that branch's filter, <strong>platform-windows.ditaval</strong>, and keeps only the Windows install row. Choose <strong>mac-</strong>, and only the macOS row is left. The topic has not changed; the filter does the work. Close the preview, and choose <code>full</code> in the status bar again before you continue.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Build</strong> Choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Build Deliverables...</strong> and click <strong>Build All</strong>. <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong> also builds every deliverable, and checks the project and the built pages as well. From the command line, the same full check is:
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml check ."} lang="bash" />
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean, with warnings\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:27] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:34] — nothing references it\n  unused key: podcast-workflow  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:50] — nothing references it\nbuild    full                 ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/full\n  5 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    beginner-mac         ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/beginner-mac\nbuild    beginner-windows     ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/beginner-windows\nbuild    podcaster-linux      ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/podcaster-linux\nbuild    review               ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/review\n  4 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\nbuild    install-variants     ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/install-variants\n  5 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\noutput   clean (full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants)\nReady: the project is healthy, every deliverable built, and the output of full, beginner-mac, beginner-windows, podcaster-linux, review, install-variants holds together. 3 unused keys above: worth knowing, and not treated as failures."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The new filters use only controlled values: the full check includes the controlled values from stage 15, and it reads the DITAVAL files too.</p>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the output</strong> <code>out/install-variants/topics/</code> has three copies of each of the two topics:
      <CodeBlock code={"win-installing-audacity.html\nwin-recording-your-first-track.html\nmac-installing-audacity.html\nmac-recording-your-first-track.html\ninstalling-audacity-linux.html\nrecording-your-first-track-linux.html"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>and the table of contents in <code>index.html</code> lists <em>Installing Audacity</em> and <em>Recording your first track</em> three times, in that order. Open <code>win-installing-audacity.html</code> and choose <strong>View</strong> &gt; <strong>Preview in Tab</strong> to see it as a browser shows it: the choice table has the <code>.exe</code> row only; <code>installing-audacity-linux.html</code> has the <code>apt install</code> row, and inside a variant the links stay in it: <code>win-recording-your-first-track.html</code> links to <code>win-installing-audacity.html</code>.</p>
      <p>The folder also holds pages the map never lists, <code>what-is-digital-audio.html</code>, <code>trimming-audio.html</code> and the rest, and an unprefixed <code>installing-audacity.html</code> with all three rows. The two branch topics link to other topics by <code>@href</code>, and DITA-OT writes every link target it can reach, once and unfiltered. A link by <code>@href</code> into the branch reaches the original, not a variant.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test conflicting output names. Change the Linux branch's <code>&lt;dvrResourceSuffix&gt;</code> to <code>&lt;dvrResourcePrefix&gt;mac-&lt;/dvrResourcePrefix&gt;</code>, the same prefix as the Mac branch, and list the branches:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"win-                 filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-windows.ditaval  keyscope=win.\nmac-                 filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-mac.ditaval  keyscope=mac.\nmac-                 filters topics/installing-audacity.dita ditaval=filters/platform-linux.ditaval  keyscope=linux.\n3 branch variant(s)."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Two variants now want the same file names. DITA-OT logs no error and no warning, and the output has no Linux pages at all. <code>mac-installing-audacity.html</code> is the Linux copy (its choice table has the <code>apt install</code> row), the Mac copy is gone, and the table of contents links the Mac variant to generated names for pages that were never written. A build alone does not show the problem, so run the full check: choose <strong>Project</strong> &gt; <strong>Check Project</strong>, or check this deliverable only with <code>dogsbay-xml check --deliverable=install-variants .</code>. The build succeeds, and the output check finds the two table of contents links. The output looks like this example:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"health   clean, with warnings\n  unused key: start-here  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:27] — nothing references it\n  unused key: digital-audio  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:34] — nothing references it\n  unused key: podcast-workflow  [/home/you/my-audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:50] — nothing references it\nbuild    install-variants     ok  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/install-variants\n  7 note(s) — run with --verbose to see them\noutput   2 broken link(s)\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/install-variants/index.html:23  @href=\"e676c532f446de854f19d505d53ab754fc11517b-1.html\" — there is no e676c532f446de854f19d505d53ab754fc11517b-1.html\n  /home/you/my-audacity-guide/out/install-variants/index.html:24  @href=\"397e15314df15a1ce6ffe81cf005134f385e5428-1.html\" — there is no 397e15314df15a1ce6ffe81cf005134f385e5428-1.html\nNot ready: 2 links in the built output lead nowhere."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The generated names and line numbers can differ between runs. The check reports the symptom, two links that lead nowhere, and not the cause. Check the <code>list-branches</code> output, and the output folder, whenever you add a variant.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and check again. Confirm that the check reports <code>Ready</code> before you continue.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;ditavalref&gt;</code> under a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code>: one filters the branch in place, several copy it once per DITAVAL.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;ditavalmeta&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;dvrResourcePrefix&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;dvrResourceSuffix&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;dvrKeyscopePrefix&gt;</code> names the copies and their key scopes; the prefixes must differ.</li>
      <li>A branch-filtered map needs no DITAVAL in its deliverable; a collision between variants builds without an error, and only the output check sees the links it breaks.</li>
      <li><code>dogsbay-xml list-branches &lt;map&gt;</code> enumerates the variants.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="next-lesson" class="group scroll-mt-20">Next lesson<a href="#next-lesson" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
